    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Status of Implementation Progress: 1. Electricity transmission capacity in project areas strengthened and modernized by 2026: Automation of 39 existing existing grid substations is ongoing. 132 kV transmission lines (Dandakhet-Rahughat, Ghorahi-Madichaur, Borang-Lapang, Nepalgunj-Kohalpur, and Chovar-Lagankhel) and 220 kV transmission line (LapangRatmate) are under construction. The associated substations of these transmission lines at Dandakhet, Rahughat, Madichaur, Nepalgunj, Lagankhel, Borang, and Lapang are also under construction. 132 kV substations at Mulpani and Dumkibas are being constructed.

2. Electricity distribution system in project areas strengthened and modernized by 2026: Distribution command and control center in Kathmandu has been completed. Substations for distribution of electricity in Borang, Keraun, Madichaur, and Pantan are ongoing. Construction of distribution lines in Morang is also ongoing.

3. Capacity of NEA to implement its corporate development plan strengthened by 2026: Training and other programs are being planned and delivered.</narrative>
    </title>
